  "id": "incentive-motivation",
  "term": "incentive motivation",
  "definition": "Incentive motivation refers to the mental processing involved in being motivated by incentives. The source notes that this processing can be abnormal in first-episode psychosis and suggests this may be linked to dopamine dysfunction rather than to general cognitive impairment.",
